      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Gumtown after pioneer Henry “Gum” Nolf, the town became Bethlehem and later added “New” to avoid confusion with eastern Pennsylvania’s Bethlehem.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
