      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Bethlehem%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In its early days, New Bethlehem boasted a lumber company, sawmill, brewery, grain mill, bank, and railroad station that served the Redbank Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.newbethlehemboro.com/about/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Smucker’s peanut butter factory in New Bethlehem sponsors the town’s annual Peanut Butter Festival, celebrating 30 years in 2025.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
